"Stewards of Intangible Cultural Heritage 2024 - Pek Sin Choon - YouTube (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-Fa4oH-TbGA)\nciteturn7youtube12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; # Stewards of Intangible Cultural Heritage 2024 - Pek Sin Choon\n# Stewards of Intangible Cultural Heritage 2024 - Pek Sin Choon\nBy: Roots Sg (11900 followers, Verified)\nPublished: 2025-04-04, 56059 views, 12 likes\n\n## Description\nPek Sin Choon stands as one of Singapore's oldest Chinese tea merchants. Established in 1925, the company is led by fourth-generation owner and tea master Mr Kenry Peh. Since the 1990s, it has also served as a key tea supplier to the bak kut teh (pork rib soup) market. Today, the tea merchant conducts workshops, tea appreciation sessions, as well as regular heritage tours to educate visitors about the history and production processes of Nanyang tea. They also actively collaborate with arts and cultural institutions, charities, and private entities, to create bespoke tea blends. The company extends its expertise by mentoring the younger generation of tea enthusiasts and collaborating with schools and Institutes of Higher Learning to document skills in tea re-firing and blending.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBest Singapore eats: Kym Ng tries Pek Sin Choon tea and Ng Ah Sio bak kut teh - YouTube (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8MEBn2fLVPY)\nciteturn7youtube13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.5 years ago; # Best Singapore eats: Kym Ng tries Pek Sin Choon tea and Ng Ah Sio bak kut teh ... 00:51 Pek Sin Choon\n# Best Singapore eats: Kym Ng tries Pek Sin Choon tea and Ng Ah Sio bak kut teh\nBy: CNA (3230000 followers, Verified)\nPublished: 2024-05-08, 21829 views, 109 likes\n\n## Description\nIn this instalment of Makan Kakis, Mediacorp Gold 905 DJ Denise Tan is joined by actress-host Kym Ng and they both find out how bak kut teh and Nanyang tea are inextricably linked in Singapore's F&B history. Read more: UR