&B company out of their predicament when money is tight, and they need an extra pair of eyes. Get in touch with me. My number is 98352535. Text me and tell me who u are and what operational help u need. Nothing is too small to ask for help. It is free, of course. But as I am still working and running a bakery business now, I may not be able to help as immediately, but I will definitely reply and see how to work around my schedule to help u. Take care, and I look forward to hearing from you.\n\n  * Terry Tng (Him/He) liked this\n\nTerry Tng (Him/He) liked this\n\nKah Seng Loh\n\n### Kah Seng Loh\n\n11mo\n\nTerry Tng (Him/He) liked this\n\nPEH KENRY explains how 白新春茶庄 Pek Sin Choon Pte Ltd's Nanyang tea was part of the experiences of Chinese immigrants to Singapore, and how it broke into the bak kut teh business. Spotify | https://lnkd.in/gpJXXvH9 YouTube | https://lnkd.in/g8BzhqeR Welcome to Chronicles of Old Singapore. This is Dr Loh KS, the people’s historian, and I talk about my research on the little histories of Singapore.\n\nKenry Peh – Pek Sin Choon & Nanyang Tea Part 2 | Chronicles of Old Singapore\n\nKenry Peh – Pek Sin Choon & Nanyang Tea Part 2 | Chronicles of Old Singapore\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYear of the Iron Ahat · Championing Bak Kut Teh Tea Culture in Singapore |Tony Johor Kaki Travels for Food · Heritage · Culture · History (https://johorkaki.blogspot.com/2024/03/origin-of-bak-kut-teh-tea-culture-in.html)\nciteturn7search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; YouTube video player ... The story of Pek Sin Choon as related by Kenry Peh is supported by this article published in Nanyang Siang Pau in 1934.\n\nSource: Nanyang Siang Pau 1949\n\nIron Arhat was followed by a series of premium tea blends, culminating in the Unknown Fragrance in 1950, specially formulated for bak kut teh.\n\nThough the custom emerged in the 1920s, we can say that popularising eating bak kut teh with premium Chinese tea appreciation can be credited to the business savvy of Pek Sin Choon.\n\nThe bak kut teh and tea sessions are relaxing, friendly meet ups among friends and business associates where ideas and opportunities are shared. It is a culture which Kenry Peh (fourth generation of Pek Sin Choon) is still actively promoting by living it out on a daily basis on his bak kut teh and tea rounds with his friends and clients.\n\nHistory of Bak Kut Teh from Coolie's Tonic to a President's Favourite 👈 click\n\nThe packaging of Wuyi Iron Arhat departed from the traditional images of deities such as Guanyin, Jigong, etc. Instead, it showed a strong, muscular man juggling iron balls.\n\nYouTube video player\n\nAt that time, the Jinan Incident of 1928 in Shandong province of China was causing indignation in British Malaya. Japanese army clashed with Chinese troops at Jinan, killed the Chinese negotiating team, and launched its invasion of China.\n\nThe muscular man motif depicts the need to be strong, fit and healthy to face the challenges of life as an individual (and also as a country).\n\nTill today, Pek Sin Choon is still the leading tea merchant in Singapore supplying bak kut teh restaurants in Singapore. Unknown Fragrance is still the preferred tea of bak kut teh and tea enthusiasts.\n\nWritten by Tony Boey on 25 Mar 2024\n\nYouTube video player\n\nKenry Peh on the beginnings of Pek Sin Choon--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBukit Brown Spirit Film Festival 2024 (https://mymindisrojak.blogspot.com/2024/08/bukit-brown-spirit-film-festival-2024.html)\nciteturn7search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.2 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; During the intermission, Blend B, a tea specially made by Pek Sin Choon (a Chinese tea specialist based in Chinatown) was served to those present.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPresented by (https://ttp-website-prod.s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com/files/2024LWM-E-programme--FA--BfpXfX0vT7qW.pdf)\nciteturn7search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; Crawled: 2.0 years ago; - PEK SIN CHOON / SINCE 1925 ... Social media icons shown: Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, WeChat, Weibo, YouTube.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNew scheme to support and grow Singapore’s heritage brands opens for nominations | The Straits Times (https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/new-scheme-to-support-and-grow-singapores-heritage-brands-opens-for-nominations)\nciteturn7search8 [wordlim: 25] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; Regunarth Siva Thyagarajan of Jothi Store and Flower Shop, Mr Kenny Peh of Pek Sin Choon and Mr Muhammad Hazmi Zin of Rumah Makan Minang, at the launch of the new pilot SG Heritage Business Scheme for long-standing local heritage businesses on March 19, 2025.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHo Yeah! Festival · Reconnecting with my Roots with Toisan Cuisine @ Granny's Secret 好嘢节·台山美食 |Tony Johor Kaki Travels for Food · Heritage · Culture · History (https://johorkaki.blogspot.com/2021/12/ho-yeah-festival-reconnecting-with-my.html)\nciteturn7search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; YouTube video player ... tea (which I was drinking in the clip) is created by Lynn and blended by Pek Sin Choon Tea Merchants.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHistory of Song Fa ● Singapore Bak Kut Teh Trend Setter |Tony Johor Kaki Travels for Food · Heritage · Culture · History (https://johorkaki.blogspot.com/2023/04/history-of-song-fa-singapore-bak-kut.html)\nciteturn7search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Song Fa founder Yeo Eng Song has been partnering Pek Sin Choon Tea Merchants since the 70s. ... YouTube video player\n-----------------------------------------------------